WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy- and Golden Globe

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
nominated actor
you know from "The Outsiders

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
and "Wayne's world"
and shows such as

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The West Wing" and
"Parks and Recreation."

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:12.445
He stars in "9-1-1: Lone Star,
which airs Monday nights on Fox.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:15.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
our friend Rob Lowe.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Rob?
-Hey, Seth!

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:19.386 size:88% position:44%
Gosh! It's been forever.
Good to see you again.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.121 line:92%
-It has been a very long time.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
How have you held up
during our pandemic year?

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:31.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, my ice-cream addictio
has gotten out of control.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:35.101
But I'm going to rehab.
So it's going to be good.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
I plan to fight it.
I'm going to fight it.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:40.473
-Well, I think that everybody,
as they've watched your body

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
not change
for the last 30 years,

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.843 line:92%
we definitely have thought

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
"There's a guy
who eats too much ice cream.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:49.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Well, you know
I try to keep my act together.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:52.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want this COVID thin
to be over like the rest of us

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:57.724
I'm lucky that I've been abl
to work and shoot the show

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.693 line:92%
I've had more nasal swabs

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
than any human
should be subjected to.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
There should be a Geneva code,
I would think.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-A lot of swabbing.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of swabbing over here,
as well.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.271 line:92%
This show must be fun to do.

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to ask, one,
about the show,

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I also want to ask
how it is --

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
your son is a writer
on the show.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-That's so cool.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:25.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My son actually
started writing --

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:28.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
working with Ryan Murphy
before I did.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.522 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And then when this --

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
When we teamed up
to do "9-1-1: Lone Star,"

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were like, "Wait a minute
Shouldn't we actually have

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:38.698
Rob Lowe's son writing on a show
about a father and a son?"

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:42.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they switched him over
from "American Horror Story"

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.136 size:88% position:44% line:92%
where he was originally,

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:46.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now he just wrote
our last crossover episode

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
where all the shows
came together,

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:51.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was our biggest episode
of the year.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did either of you
have any trepidation about

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
working together,
or was it just pure enthusiasm

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.454
-I actually lo-- I thought
it would be great, actually.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's --
I've got to tell you, as a dad

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.128
it's been so fun when he'll come
and give me a note

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.262 line:92%
and the note will be great

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he's a smart littl
whipper-snapper.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't even realize
it's my own son.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:16.035 size:78% position:39%
And then I walk away,
I go, "Wait a minute!

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to change
that kid's diapers!

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.506 line:92%
What the hell's goin' on?"

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do want to give him credi
because --

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's obviously
a wonderful TV writer,

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we've talked about
how he trolls your Instagram

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that might be some
of my favorite writing of his.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's one
you posted of yourself

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.788 line:92%
and you wrote, "Backyard vibes."

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:36.956 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And then your son wrote,

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:40.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're this close
to losing phone privileges."

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughter ]
-I like that one.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:46.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's this -- There was
a "West Wing," and he wrote,

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We all know you don't kno
how to play chess."

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this, Rob --
this is the kill shot.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:57.710
You wrote, "I love that ancestry
connects my passions of history,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
family, and storytelling,"
and your son wrote,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.885
"I used it to find out tha
my real dad was John Stamos.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:09.522 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.058 line:92%
I mean, those are all A-plus

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right?
-Yeah.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it's -- Well,
I'm glad you think he's funny,

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:19.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause we were taking out
a big comedy pitch this week

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I have
the Seth Meyers approval.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love this.
-Great. Yes, please.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
Feel free to drop my name
if you think

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's at all helpful
in any pitches.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this is --
This show, "9-1-1,"

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.078 line:92%
this is obviously not a comedy

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:37.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play a New York firema
transplanted to Austin, Texas.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
And are you enjoying
doing this show?

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:42.655
It seems like an incredibl
meaty part to be playing.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.958 line:92%
-Yeah, I'm loving it. And I'm --

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.827
Look, we all know how hard it is
to be in a show

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
that actually works
and people -- that's a hit

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:51.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's fun.
I've got to tell you.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really fun
that it's been embraced.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:58.004
And I think there's somethin
about playing real-life heroes

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.172 line:92%
first responders in a time

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:03.109
where we're so grateful
that they're actually out there.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:07.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I love doing that.
I love that it's physical.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love that the tone
is so weird.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it's a Ryan Murphy
version, you know?

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:15.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not your parents'
"Emergency!"

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that keeps it
really fun for me.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned
that it's really physical.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.760 size:84% position:42%
How have you done with
the physical challenges

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.329 line:92%
of pretending to be a fireman?

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:27.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As you know, I can preten
to do many things.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:27.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:31.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But don't ask me
to actually save anybody

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:33.039 size:88% position:44% line:92%
or do anything for real.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:36.843
But when it comes to fake stuff,
I'm so good at it.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughter ]
-You know, so...

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:42.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that
I was kind of born --

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.883
[ Laughs ]
I was born to play this fireman.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:49.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
I definitely look way more
realistic doing it than I feel

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:50.690 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
You also became a podcaste
during this past year.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Literally! With Rob Lowe"
is your podcast.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
this is both in reference

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
to your "Parks and Rec"
character,

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also a chance for you
to sort of do

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.572 line:92%
some longer-form talking stuff

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you enjoyed it?
-I loved it.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to say
I thought I might like it,

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it turns out
I really love it.

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:16.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
And whether it's getting,
you know, people

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have been
in the public eye forever

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I've known
in a different way

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:25.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
like Gwyneth Paltrow or Pratt,
Chris Pratt, you know.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:28.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's being able to talk to the
and about them

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.330
in a way
that other people probably can't

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they don't have
that history.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's been awesome.
I love it.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love the long-form
conversation.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.170 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-You mentioned Pratt.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.972
I think that "Parks and Rec,
as well as "The West Wing" -

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:43.409
I should note you have two shows
that I think provided

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.578
great comfort to people,
especially this last year

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:48.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
when everyone was looking
for things to watch.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:50.583 line:92%
People must always want to kno

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:55.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you are still in touch
with those two casts.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:55.488 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:59.258
I am in touch more I would say
with the "Parks and Rec" cast,

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:02.428
and I think that's probabl
a function of that it's --

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't 20 -- "West Wing
is almost 20 years ago.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's crazy.
-That's insane to say that

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:13.106 size:84% position:42%
But I was just texting
with one of the writers

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.273 size:75% position:38% line:92%
on the staff, Aaron.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:21.080
I hosted a big "Chicago 7" panel
for Aaron Sorkin,

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.249 size:88% position:44% line:92%
who I continue to adore.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:25.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so whenever I see
any of the gang

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:27.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
from either show,
it's always great.

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:29.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's really hard
when everybody's so busy.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:31.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and on the other hand
it's also good

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
that everybody is busy,
and we certainly appreciat

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you made time for us
on your schedule.

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always great
to see you, Rob.

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you too.
You're killing it.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:40.933 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Keep up the good work.

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll tell you who's
killing it, is your son.

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.737 line:92%
You go sell that comedy pitch.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm gonna go sell it, baby!
-Okay.

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you don't sell it,
it's on you.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:50.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause he's the star.
-Not on him. It'll be on me.

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:54.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"9-1-1: Lone Star"
airs Monday nights on Fox.

